I'll re-apply the app-params persistence changes on top of the current version of `src/store/ui.js` (which has since gained the `isSidebarExpanded` getter and the sidebar collapse controls).

## 1. Analysis & Pre-Thinking

**Core Requirements**
When an app that is **already open** receives new params, that change must survive a reload. In this codebase "saving the view" means persisting the dockview layout (`views` store → `localStorage['projectLayout_<project>']`), which is the only place open apps/panels are stored (`uiState` deliberately strips `openApps`).

**Where params live (two places, must stay in sync)**
- `state.openApps[tabId].params` → read by components through the `$app` mixin.
- The hosting dockview panel params → what dockview's `toJSON()` serializes into the saved layout.

**Gap found in the current file**
`updateAppParams` still carries the inline merge + panel-sync + persist logic, and the two early-return branches in `showApp()` (`existingApp`, `existingPanel`) **silently drop** the incoming params — so re-opening an already-open app with new params (e.g. a file viewer with a different `filePath`) loses that change on reload.

**Strategic approach**
Extract the existing logic into one module-scope helper `applyAppParams(app, params, panel)` and use it from both `updateAppParams` and the two `showApp` early-return branches — a single place decides when the view is saved.

**Dependencies & risks**
- `$storex.views.onLayoutChanged()` is a safe no-op when there is no desktop API / no loaded layout (mobile, vibe mode).
- No-op updates are skipped so we don't persist pointlessly → no layout-change event loops.

**Target files**
- `src/store/ui.js` (only file changed).

## 2. Minimum Changes Approach

`src/store/ui.js`
- Add module helper `applyAppParams(app, params, panel)` (guards, merge, mirror, persist).
- `updateAppParams` mutation delegates to it (same behaviour, no duplication).
- `showApp` early-return branches apply the incoming params before returning, so params of an already-open app are kept **and saved**.

## 3. File changes

